    "description": "Medical Properties Partnership is a joint venture that owns eight Massachusetts general acute care hospitals. Its end market is healthcare infrastructure, with cash flows tied to leased hospital real estate operated by healthcare providers rather than direct clinical service delivery. The operating model is asset-heavy and contracted, centered on essential hospital properties with long-term rental income and infrastructure-like real estate characteristics. Macquarie and Medical Properties Trust stated in 2021 and 2022 that the transaction covered eight Steward-operated hospitals in Massachusetts at a portfolio value of approximately $1.78 billion. A Macquarie Infrastructure Partners V-controlled subsidiary completed the acquisition of a 50 percent interest in the portfolio in March 2022, leaving Medical Properties Trust with the remaining 50 percent stake.",
